content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-24020",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 92 °C and rising. The applicable HF-300 housing-surface limits are normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reading is therefore 22 °C above the normal maximum, 12 °C above alarm and 2 °C above trip. Because it is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift; continued operation is not appropriate with the trip limit already exceeded.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using Figure 3's bearing-housing vibration-velocity criterion, the reported 4.0 mm/s is above the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 mm/s RMS Zone B/C boundary, placing it in Zone B, 'Long-term operation'. It is not in restricted Zone C or highest-severity Zone D, so this reading alone does not trigger SSP-07's highest-zone immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification rule. This classification assumes the report represents the RMS bearing-housing velocity required by the manual.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The noisy bearing is a qualitative symptom rather than a reading with a numerical limit. The bearing-replacement procedure expressly treats bearing noise or high temperature as a trigger to replace both bearings as a pair; the reported drive-end bearing has both symptoms.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear or damage is most likely because bearing wear is listed for both high bearing temperature and high vibration, and the accompanying noise and temperature also directly invoke the paired-bearing replacement procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is also a common cause of both high bearing temperature and high vibration and must be checked.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing can explain the high bearing temperature; check the grease quantity rather than assuming wear is the only cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation remain possible contributors to the vibration; inspect the impeller and check NPSH as part of diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediately confirm whether P-110 has tripped. If it is still running, stop it now and prevent restart because the rising 92 °C housing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's 90 °C trip limit. Raise this P1 work order within the shift as required for temperature above the 80 °C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal work, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the pump; then obtain the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the symptoms before reassembly: check grease quantity, check alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller for wear or damage, and check NPSH for possible cavitation. Record which of the listed probable causes are confirmed or eliminated.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Where bearing or impeller access requires removal of the rotating assembly, use the back pull-out arrangement, which permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so use a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings as a pair using HF3-512 and HF3-510. Do not replace only the noisy, hot drive-end bearing: the manual requires paired replacement when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened. During reassembly, use Table 5 torques with lightly oiled threads on fasteners actually disturbed: bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm if removed; and seal gland nuts M10 to 25 Nm only if the seal gland is disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any running test, restore the specified Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. On controlled recommissioning, monitor bearing-housing surface temperature and noise against the 70/80/90 °C normal/alarm/trip limits. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3; if it is classified in Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace as one half of the mandatory bearing pair because the drive-end bearing is noisy and above the high-temperature limits.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing even if this bearing shows no separate symptom.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; have one available and fit it whenever the casing is opened for inspection or repair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Apply priority-1 handling within the shift because the bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's 80 °C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, use electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For lifting the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment; the mass exceeds SSP-07's 25 kg threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before line break, confirm whether P-110 is on a chemically dosed line. If it is, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory. The supplied dosing statement specifically identifies P-101 to P-106 as sodium-hypochlorite-dosed but does not establish P-110's service.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current 4.0 mm/s reading is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone. If subsequent testing classifies the highest bearing-housing reading in Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment after bearing-housing or motor movement: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does the reported 4.0 mm/s represent RMS vibration velocity, on which bearing housing was it measured, and is it the highest of readings from both housings? The manual's zone classification requires bearing-housing RMS velocity and classification of the highest reading (C06, C07).",
    "What liquid service is P-110 on, and is its line chemically dosed? C16 identifies only P-101 to P-106 as sodium-hypochlorite-dosed, so it cannot determine whether the chemical goggles and nitrile-gloves control applies to P-110 (C15, C16).",
    "What grease type, specified grease quantity and detailed bearing-installation requirements apply? The troubleshooting table says to check grease quantity, but the supplied evidence gives neither the correct quantity nor a grease specification or detailed bearing-fitting procedure (C09, C10).",
    "What are the inspection results for bearing condition, grease quantity, alignment, impeller condition and NPSH? These are needed to establish the final root cause and whether any additional parts, such as an impeller or seal components, are required; no such parts are authorised by the current symptoms alone (C09).",
    "The standard labour table provides no durations for troubleshooting, grease checks, NPSH investigation, impeller inspection or any additional repairs. The listed labour therefore covers only paired bearing replacement and laser alignment (C12)."
  ]
}
